#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Latar belakang {#background}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every IBM Quantum&reg; QPU reports a set of properties that describe how well each of its qubits is currently working: relaxation times ($T_1$), coherence times ($T_2$), readout errors, and one- and two-qubit gate errors. These numbers matter in practice. The transpiler uses them to decide which physical qubits your circuit should run on, error mitigation techniques rely on them, and you might use them to judge whether a device is working well enough for an experiment.\n"
msgstr "Setiap QPU IBM Quantum&reg; melaporkan satu set ciri yang menerangkan sebaik mana setiap qubitnya berfungsi pada masa ini: masa relaksasi ($T_1$), masa koheren ($T_2$), ralat bacaan, dan ralat get satu- dan dua-qubit. Nombor ini penting dalam praktiknya. Transpiler menggunakannya untuk menentukan qubit fizikal mana yang sepatutnya menjalankan litar anda, teknik mitigasi ralat bergantung padanya, dan anda mungkin menggunakannya untuk menilai sama ada peranti berfungsi cukup baik untuk sesuatu eksperimen.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The reported properties come from calibration procedures that typically run about once a day. Superconducting qubits, however, can drift on shorter timescales, and transient defects (so-called two-level systems) can temporarily degrade a qubit that looked excellent at calibration time. In addition, a job is often transpiled well before it actually executes, so decisions based on the reported properties can rest on stale information. The tutorial [Real-time benchmarking for qubit selection](/tutorials/real-time-benchmarking-for-qubit-selection) shows how much these properties can fluctuate from day to day, and builds a full characterization workflow by hand from individual [Qiskit Experiments](https://qiskit-community.github.io/qiskit-experiments/).\n"
msgstr "Ciri yang dilaporkan berasal daripada prosedur kalibrasi yang biasanya dijalankan kira-kira sekali sehari. Qubit superkonduktor, bagaimanapun, boleh hanyut pada skala masa yang lebih pendek, dan kecacatan sementara (dipanggil sistem dua-aras) boleh sementara merosotkan qubit yang kelihatan cemerlang pada masa kalibrasi. Tambahan pula, tugasan sering ditranspilasi jauh sebelum ia benar-benar dilaksanakan, jadi keputusan berdasarkan ciri yang dilaporkan boleh bergantung pada maklumat lapuk. Tutorial [Penanda arasan masa-nyata untuk pemilihan qubit](/tutorials/real-time-benchmarking-for-qubit-selection) menunjukkan sejauh mana ciri ini boleh berubah-ubah dari hari ke hari, dan membina aliran kerja pencirian penuh secara manual daripada [Qiskit Experiments](https://qiskit-community.github.io/qiskit-experiments/) individu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial shows the streamlined version of that workflow, by using the `BackendCharacterization` utility from [Qiskit Device Benchmarking](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qiskit-device-benchmarking), which packages the experiment construction, job submission, and curve fitting into a few calls. You spend roughly 70 seconds of QPU time and get back a backend object whose properties reflect the device *right now*, ready to be compared against the reported values or passed on to downstream tools.\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini menunjukkan versi teragih aliran kerja tersebut, dengan menggunakan utiliti `BackendCharacterization` daripada [Qiskit Device Benchmarking](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qiskit-device-benchmarking), yang membungkus pembinaan eksperimen, penghantaran tugasan, dan penyesuaian lengkung ke dalam beberapa panggilan. Anda menghabiskan kira-kira 70 saat masa QPU dan mendapatkan kembali objek backend yang ciri-cirinya mencerminkan peranti *pada masa ini*, sedia untuk dibandingkan dengan nilai yang dilaporkan atau dihantar ke alat hiliran.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The characterization experiments {#the-characterization-experiments}"
msgstr "Eksperimen pencirian {#the-characterization-experiments}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The suite measures five properties, each with a standard experiment:\n"
msgstr "Suite ini mengukur lima ciri, setiap satu dengan eksperimen standard:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Readout error** (`readout`): Each qubit is prepared in $|0\\rangle$ or $|1\\rangle$ and immediately measured. The probability of reading out the wrong state gives the state preparation and measurement (SPAM) error.\n"
msgstr "**Ralat bacaan** (`readout`): Setiap qubit disediakan dalam $|0\\rangle$ atau $|1\\rangle$ dan segera diukur. Kebarangkalian membaca keadaan yang salah memberikan ralat penyediaan keadaan dan pengukuran (SPAM).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Single-qubit gate error** (`rb_1q`): Randomized benchmarking (RB) runs sequences of random single-qubit Clifford gates that ideally compose to the identity. The way the survival probability decays with sequence length yields the average error per gate, independent of SPAM errors.\n"
msgstr "**Ralat get satu-qubit** (`rb_1q`): Penanda arasan rawak (RB) menjalankan urutan get Clifford satu-qubit rawak yang secara ideal terkompos kepada identiti. Cara kebarangkalian kelangsungan mereput dengan panjang urutan menghasilkan purata ralat setiap get, tidak bergantung pada ralat SPAM.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Two-qubit gate error** (`rb_2q`): The same RB idea applied to full layers of non-overlapping two-qubit gates executed simultaneously, as in a [layer fidelity](https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.05933) experiment. Because many gates run at once, the resulting error rates include crosstalk effects and are closer to what a deep circuit actually experiences.\n"
msgstr "**Ralat get dua-qubit** (`rb_2q`): Idea RB yang sama digunakan pada lapisan penuh get dua-qubit yang tidak bertindih yang dilaksanakan serentak, seperti dalam eksperimen [kesetiaan lapisan](https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.05933). Kerana banyak get berjalan sekaligus, kadar ralat yang terhasil termasuk kesan crosstalk dan lebih hampir kepada apa yang dialami sebenarnya oleh litar yang dalam.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**$T_1$** (`t1`): Each qubit is excited and measured after increasing delays. The decay of the excited-state population gives the relaxation time.\n"
msgstr "**$T_1$** (`t1`): Setiap qubit dieksitasikan dan diukur selepas kelewatan yang meningkat. Peruputan populasi keadaan tereksitasi memberikan masa relaksasi.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**$T_2$** (`t2`): A Hahn echo experiment puts each qubit in a superposition, applies an echo pulse halfway through a delay, and measures how quickly phase coherence is lost. By default a single echo is used; a multi-echo (CPMG-style) variant is demonstrated at the end of this tutorial.\n"
msgstr "**$T_2$** (`t2`): Eksperimen gema Hahn meletakkan setiap qubit dalam superposisi, menggunakan denyut gema di pertengahan kelewatan, dan mengukur seberapa cepat koheren fasa hilang. Secara lalai satu gema digunakan; varian pelbagai-gema (bergaya CPMG) ditunjukkan di penghujung tutorial ini.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "What refreshing does and does not do {#what-refreshing-does-and-does-not-do}"
msgstr "Apa yang dilakukan dan tidak dilakukan oleh penyegaran {#what-refreshing-does-and-does-not-do}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keep three points in mind when using this workflow:\n"
msgstr "Ingat tiga perkara ini apabila menggunakan aliran kerja ini:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The refreshed properties live only in the backend object returned to you. Nothing changes on the device itself or in the calibration data that IBM Quantum reports to other users.\n"
msgstr "Ciri yang disegarkan hanya wujud dalam objek backend yang dikembalikan kepada anda. Tiada apa yang berubah pada peranti itu sendiri atau dalam data kalibrasi yang dilaporkan oleh IBM Quantum kepada pengguna lain.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The measured values are a snapshot taken with a particular methodology. Some of them, notably the layered two-qubit errors and the parallel single-echo $T_2$ values, are measured differently from the reported calibration data, so part of any gap you observe is methodological rather than drift. This tutorial points out where that happens.\n"
msgstr "Nilai yang diukur adalah gambaran seketika yang diambil dengan metodologi tertentu. Sebahagian daripadanya, terutamanya ralat dua-qubit berlapis dan nilai $T_2$ gema-tunggal selari, diukur secara berbeza daripada data kalibrasi yang dilaporkan, jadi sebahagian daripada apa jua jurang yang anda perhatikan adalah bersifat metodologi dan bukannya hanyutan. Tutorial ini menunjukkan di mana perkara itu berlaku.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The characterization itself costs QPU time (about 70 seconds for the full suite on a Heron r2 processor), which is the price of up-to-date information.\n"
msgstr "Pencirian itu sendiri memerlukan masa QPU (kira-kira 70 saat untuk suite penuh pada pemproses Heron r2), yang merupakan kos untuk mendapatkan maklumat terkini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The workflow follows the four steps of a Qiskit pattern:\n"
msgstr "Aliran kerja ini mengikuti empat langkah corak Qiskit:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem.** Choose the device and the set of properties to measure.\n"
msgstr "**Langkah 1: Petakan input klasik kepada masalah kuantum.** Pilih peranti dan set ciri untuk diukur.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution.** The utility builds the experiment circuits directly in the device's native gates and parallelizes them across the chip.\n"
msgstr "**Langkah 2: Optimumkan masalah untuk pelaksanaan perkakasan kuantum.** Utiliti ini membina litar eksperimen terus dalam get asli peranti dan menyelarikannya merentas cip.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives.** The experiments run as Sampler jobs inside a batch.\n"
msgstr "**Langkah 3: Laksanakan menggunakan primitif Qiskit.** Eksperimen dijalankan sebagai tugasan Sampler di dalam kelompok.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format.** Fit the measurement data into per-qubit error maps, refresh the backend, and compare the measured properties against the reported ones.\n"
msgstr "**Langkah 4: Pasca-proses dan kembalikan keputusan dalam format klasik yang dikehendaki.** Sesuaikan data pengukuran ke dalam peta ralat setiap-qubit, segarkan backend, dan bandingkan ciri yang diukur berbanding yang dilaporkan.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Requirements {#requirements}"
msgstr "Keperluan {#requirements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before starting this tutorial, be sure you have the following installed:\n"
msgstr "Sebelum memulakan tutorial ini, pastikan anda telah memasang perkara berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit SDK v2.0 or later, with [visualization](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/visualization) support\n"
msgstr "Qiskit SDK v2.0 atau lebih baharu, dengan sokongan [visualization](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/visualization)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit Runtime v0.40 or later (`pip install qiskit-ibm-runtime`)\n"
msgstr "Qiskit Runtime v0.40 atau lebih baharu (`pip install qiskit-ibm-runtime`)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit Device Benchmarking, which also installs [Qiskit Experiments](https://qiskit-community.github.io/qiskit-experiments/) (`pip install git+https://github.com/qiskit-community/qiskit-device-benchmarking.git`)\n"
msgstr "Qiskit Device Benchmarking, yang juga memasang [Qiskit Experiments](https://qiskit-community.github.io/qiskit-experiments/) (`pip install git+https://github.com/qiskit-community/qiskit-device-benchmarking.git`)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr "Persediaan {#setup}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Import the required libraries.\n"
msgstr "Import pustaka yang diperlukan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The characterization suite builds several experiments, submits multiple jobs, and fits the results, which can take a couple of minutes in total. Enable INFO-level logging so that each stage prints its progress as it happens.\n"
msgstr "Suite pencirian membina beberapa eksperimen, menghantar berbilang job, dan memadankan keputusan, yang boleh mengambil masa beberapa minit secara keseluruhan. Aktifkan log tahap INFO supaya setiap peringkat mencetak kemajuannya semasa ia berlaku.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"
msgstr "Contoh simulator berskala kecil {#small-scale-simulator-example}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial does not include a simulator example. The workflow measures the physical imperfections of a specific device: how quickly its qubits relax and dephase, and how often its gates and readout fail. An ideal simulator has none of these imperfections, so there is nothing to characterize. You could attach a synthetic noise model to a fake backend, but the experiments would then only recover the numbers you put in yourself. For that reason, we proceed directly to hardware, broken into the four steps of a Qiskit pattern.\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini tidak mengandungi contoh simulator. Aliran kerja ini mengukur kecacatan fizikal sesuatu peranti tertentu: seberapa cepat qubitnya berehat dan menyahfasa, dan seberapa kerap gate serta bacaannya gagal. Simulator ideal tidak mempunyai sebarang kecacatan ini, jadi tiada apa untuk dicirikan. Anda boleh melampirkan model hingar sintetik kepada backend palsu, tetapi eksperimen kemudiannya hanya akan memulihkan nombor yang anda sendiri masukkan. Atas sebab itu, kami terus ke perkakasan, dipecahkan kepada empat langkah corak Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr "Contoh perkakasan berskala besar {#large-scale-hardware-example}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Memetakan input klasik kepada masalah kuantum {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this workflow the \"problem\" is the device itself: the classical inputs are the QPU you want to characterize and the list of properties to measure, and the quantum experiments are the characterization circuits generated from them.\n"
msgstr "Dalam aliran kerja ini, \"masalah\" ialah peranti itu sendiri: input klasik ialah QPU yang anda mahu cirikan dan senarai sifat yang hendak diukur, dan eksperimen kuantum ialah litar pencirian yang dijana daripadanya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, select a backend. This tutorial uses `ibm_kingston`, a 156-qubit Heron r2 processor; you can substitute any IBM Quantum device you have access to (or pick one with `service.least_busy()`).\n"
msgstr "Pertama, pilih backend. Tutorial ini menggunakan `ibm_kingston`, sebuah pemproses Heron r2 156-qubit; anda boleh menggantikannya dengan mana-mana peranti IBM Quantum yang anda ada akses (atau pilih satu dengan `service.least_busy()`).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, choose which properties to measure. You can pass any subset of the following experiments:\n"
msgstr "Seterusnya, pilih sifat mana yang hendak diukur. Anda boleh laluk mana-mana subset eksperimen berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`readout`: SPAM (state preparation and measurement) experiment\n"
msgstr "`readout`: eksperimen SPAM (penyediaan dan pengukuran keadaan)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`rb_1q`: isolated single-qubit randomized benchmarking\n"
msgstr "`rb_1q`: penanda aras rawak satu-qubit terasing\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`rb_2q`: simultaneous two-qubit randomized benchmarking from a layer fidelity experiment\n"
msgstr "`rb_2q`: penanda aras rawak dua-qubit serentak daripada eksperimen kesetiaan lapisan\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`t2`: $T_2$ Hahn echo experiment (a single echo by default)\n"
msgstr "`t2`: eksperimen gema Hahn $T_2$ (satu gema secara lalai)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`t1`: $T_1$ relaxation experiment\n"
msgstr "`t1`: eksperimen relaksasi $T_1$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the full suite to get a complete picture of the device; drop entries from the list if you only care about some properties and want to save QPU time.\n"
msgstr "Jalankan suite penuh untuk mendapatkan gambaran lengkap peranti; buang entri daripada senarai jika anda hanya mengambil berat tentang sesetengah sifat dan mahu menjimatkan masa QPU.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Mengoptimumkan masalah untuk pelaksanaan perkakasan kuantum {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In most tutorials this is where you would transpile your circuits. Here, `BackendCharacterization` takes care of that internally. It builds the experiment circuits directly in the device's native gates, runs the single-qubit experiments on all qubits in parallel, and schedules the two-qubit benchmarking over disjoint layers of the coupling map so that the entire device is covered with a handful of jobs. Because of this parallelization, the whole suite consumes only about 70 seconds of QPU time.\n"
msgstr "Dalam kebanyakan tutorial, di sinilah anda akan mentranspil litar anda. Di sini, `BackendCharacterization` menguruskan itu secara dalaman. Ia membina litar eksperimen terus dalam gate asli peranti, menjalankan eksperimen satu-qubit pada semua qubit secara selari, dan menjadualkan penanda aras dua-qubit merentasi lapisan berasingan peta gandingan supaya keseluruhan peranti diliputi dengan beberapa job sahaja. Disebabkan penyelarian ini, keseluruhan suite hanya mengambil kira-kira 70 saat masa QPU.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Initialize the class that manages the workflow:\n"
msgstr "Mulakan kelas yang menguruskan aliran kerja:\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Melaksanakan menggunakan primitif Qiskit {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `run_experiments` method builds the circuits and submits them as [Sampler](/guides/get-started-with-sampler) jobs. Run it inside a [`Batch`](/guides/run-jobs-batch) context so that the jobs are scheduled together on the QPU, and the method returns once all jobs have been submitted. (You can also run it outside a batch, or inside a `Session`.)\n"
msgstr "Kaedah `run_experiments` membina litar dan menghantarnya sebagai job [Sampler](/guides/get-started-with-sampler). Jalankan ia di dalam konteks [`Batch`](/guides/run-jobs-batch) supaya job dijadualkan bersama pada QPU, dan kaedah tersebut kembali sebaik sahaja semua job telah dihantar. (Anda juga boleh menjalankannya di luar batch, atau di dalam `Session`.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"You might see a warning about a backend being passed while a session context manager is open. This is expected and can be safely ignored.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The method returns the submitted jobs as a dictionary keyed by experiment, which is useful for tracking them on the [IBM Quantum Platform dashboard](/guides/monitor-job) or for debugging.\n"
msgstr "Kaedah ini mengembalikan job yang dihantar sebagai kamus yang dikunci mengikut eksperimen, yang berguna untuk menjejak mereka pada [papan pemuka IBM Quantum Platform](/guides/monitor-job) atau untuk debugging.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Memproses pasca dan mengembalikan keputusan dalam format klasik yang dikehendaki {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Analyze the results {#analyze-the-results}"
msgstr "Analisis keputusan {#analyze-the-results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `analyze_results` method waits for the jobs to finish and fits the measurement data: exponential decays for $T_1$ and $T_2$, survival-probability decays for the RB experiments, and assignment matrices for readout. It returns a dictionary of *error maps*, one entry per measured property, each mapping a qubit (or qubit pair) to its measured value.\n"
msgstr "Kaedah `analyze_results` menunggu job selesai dan memadankan data pengukuran: reputan eksponen untuk $T_1$ dan $T_2$, reputan kebarangkalian kemandirian untuk eksperimen RB, dan matriks penugasan untuk bacaan. Ia mengembalikan kamus *peta ralat*, satu entri bagi setiap sifat yang diukur, setiap satu memetakan qubit (atau pasangan qubit) kepada nilai terukurnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The maps cover readout error, the single-qubit `x` and `sx` gate errors, the layered two-qubit errors (`lf_error_map`, from the layer fidelity experiment), and the $T_1$ and $T_2$ times in seconds.\n"
msgstr "Peta tersebut meliputi ralat bacaan, ralat gate `x` dan `sx` satu-qubit, ralat dua-qubit berlapis (`lf_error_map`, daripada eksperimen kesetiaan lapisan), dan masa $T_1$ dan $T_2$ dalam saat.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Update the backend properties {#update-the-backend-properties}"
msgstr "Kemas kini sifat backend {#update-the-backend-properties}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `update_backend` method writes the measured values into the properties of a copy of the backend and returns it. The original `backend` object keeps the reported calibration data, so that we can compare the two, as shown below. Remember that this update is purely local to your Python session; it does not change anything on the device or for other users.\n"
msgstr "Kaedah `update_backend` menulis nilai terukur ke dalam sifat salinan backend dan mengembalikannya. Objek `backend` asal mengekalkan data penentukuran yang dilaporkan, supaya kita dapat membandingkan kedua-duanya, seperti yang ditunjukkan di bawah. Ingat bahawa kemas kini ini adalah semata-mata setempat kepada sesi Python anda; ia tidak mengubah apa-apa pada peranti atau untuk pengguna lain.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare the measured properties against the reported ones {#compare-the-measured-properties-against-the-reported-ones}"
msgstr "Bandingkan sifat terukur berbanding yang dilaporkan {#compare-the-measured-properties-against-the-reported-ones}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, plot the measured real-time properties against the values the backend reports. In each panel the qubits (or qubit pairs) are sorted by the measured value, so the measured curve is smooth by construction and the scatter of the reported values around it shows where the two disagree. A single plot is shown for single-qubit RB because the same measured error per gate is assigned to both the `x` and `sx` gates. Axis limits are chosen from the bulk of the data so that a few extreme outliers do not compress the plots; any points outside the range are counted in an annotation on the plot (or pass `ylim` to override the limits).\n"
msgstr "Akhir sekali, plotkan sifat masa nyata yang diukur berbanding nilai yang dilaporkan oleh backend. Dalam setiap panel, qubit (atau pasangan qubit) disusun mengikut nilai terukur, jadi lengkung terukur adalah licin secara pembinaan dan serakan nilai yang dilaporkan di sekelilingnya menunjukkan di mana kedua-duanya tidak bersetuju. Satu plot ditunjukkan untuk RB satu-qubit kerana ralat terukur yang sama bagi setiap gate diberikan kepada kedua-dua gate `x` dan `sx`. Had paksi dipilih daripada bahagian utama data supaya beberapa titik ekstrem tidak memampatkan plot; sebarang titik di luar julat dikira dalam anotasi pada plot (atau laluk `ylim` untuk mengatasi had tersebut).\n"

